.TH ANALYZE_BALANCE 1 "August 2026" "Dragon GL 2026.05.26.01" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
analyze_balance.py \- Dragon GL Combat Log Analyzer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B python3 analyze_balance.py
[\fB/path/to/combat_log.json\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B analyze_balance.py
is a statistical analysis tool for Dungeon Masters and developers of the Dragon GL engine. It parses the real-time combat log generated by \fBdragongl_server(1)\fR and produces a detailed statistical report on game balance.
.PP
The tool evaluates attack hit rates, critical hit frequencies, saving throw resistances, spell efficiencies, and overall dungeon lethality. The input file must be a valid JSON array generated by the server. If the server is stopped forcefully without proper shutdown, the JSON file might lack the closing bracket, and the tool will refuse to parse it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B /path/to/combat_log.json
Optional. The path to the combat log file. If omitted, the tool defaults to reading \fBcombat_log.json\fR in the current working directory.
.SH OUTPUT SECTIONS
The generated report is divided into four main sections:
.TP
.B ATTACK REPORT
Global attack statistics (hits, misses, crits) and a per-attacker breakdown showing total attacks, hit percentage, total damage, and average damage per hit.
.TP
.B SAVING THROW REPORT
Global saving throw pass rates and a per-effect breakdown (e.g., Fireball, Poison Gas) showing how often players and monsters successfully resisted the effect.
.TP
.B SPELL REPORT
Global spellcasting efficiency and a per-spell breakdown showing total casts, total damage/healing value, average value per cast, and resistance percentages.
.TP
.B DEATH REPORT
Global death count, a per-floor death distribution with an ASCII bar graph, and a top 15 ranking of the most lethal entities (killers) in the session.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B python3 /usr/share/dragongl/tools/analyze_balance.py
Analyze the default \fBcombat_log.json\fR in the current directory.
.TP
.B python3 /usr/share/dragongl/tools/analyze_balance.py /var/log/dragongl/session_log.json
Analyze a specific combat log file.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dragongl_server (1),
.BR dragongl_client (1)
.PP
Full documentation is available in the README.md file or online at https://github.com/nicolataibi/dragongl.
